  "body": "Local HTML View renders `.html` and `.htm` files from your vault as real pages instead of sanitized previews, so scripts run, stylesheets apply, `<canvas>` draws and click handlers respond.\n\nExisting HTML readers strip `<script>` before display. That is safe for a saved article but leaves any generated page dead: dashboards, D3 or Chart.js figures, Mermaid exports and reveal.js decks open blank.\n\n**Features**\n\n- Opens HTML files in a normal Obsidian tab with a toolbar for reload, zoom and \"open in default browser\"\n- `obsidian://`, `http://`, `https://` and `mailto:` links inside the page are handed to the OS, so deep links jump back to the right note\n- Webview renderer by default, with an iframe fallback you can force per vault\n- Takes over `.html` and `.htm` from other HTML plugins, and restores the previous owner on unload\n- No polling and no persistent timers\n\nDesktop only, because the webview renderer is an Electron element.\n\n**Install manually:** copy `main.js`, `manifest.json` and `styles.css` into `<vault>/.obsidian/plugins/local-html-view/`.\n"
